@@ -3,3 +3,23 @@
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+## Rental module
+
+`createRentalService()` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns an in-memory service:
+
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })`: `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`; `dailyPrice` is an integer in euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })`: returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })`: returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+
+School rules enforced: money in integer cents; times are UTC ISO-8601 strings (returned normalised, e.g.
+`2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z`); periods are whole days, from midnight UTC to midnight UTC, `end` being the
+start of the day after the last day (so `end` must be after `start`); an item cannot be booked for
+overlapping periods (back-to-back periods are fine). `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a
+disallowed period, and `book` throws when the item is not free. Booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, …)
+to keep the service deterministic.
+
+Not yet implemented: cancellations. The policy (no refund when cancelled less than 24 hours before the
+start, full refund otherwise) is reserved for that later work.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
